The upstream tree contains the application and optional integration patches.
The source builder derives debian/control and maintainer scripts from the same
templates used by the standalone binary builder. Both installers use the same
payload builder. The build runs isolated desktop and protocol tests, never
starts the host daemon, and never modifies host networking.

One source package builds gnome-wifi-hotspot (standalone app/service),
gnome-wifi-hotspot-gnome (optional Shell controls), and gnome-wifi-hotspot-tray
(optional StatusNotifier controls). Integrations depend on the exact app version.
The monolithic upgrade fixture in tests/build_legacy_package.py is solely for
disposable-container tests and must never be published.
